---
import LabShell from "../../components/lab/LabShell.astro";
---
<LabShell title="Controls" current="controls"
  intro="Interactive UI controls that aren't form data-entry — tabs, loading/progress indicators. None of this exists in the codebase yet; everything below is a sketch built only from existing tokens (no new colors/radii invented), so it's a starting point, not a locked design.">

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--gap">doesn't exist — sketch only</span>
    <h2>Tabs</h2>
    <p>Styled after the same mono-caps + bottom-border-on-active pattern <code>Nav</code> already uses, so it
      doesn't introduce a second "active state" convention.</p>
    <div class="lab-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Example tabs">
      <button class="lab-tab active" role="tab" aria-selected="true" type="button">Overview</button>
      <button class="lab-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" type="button">Projects</button>
      <button class="lab-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" type="button">Finances</button>
      <button class="lab-tab" role="tab" aria-selected="false" type="button" disabled>Archived</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--gap">doesn't exist — sketch only</span>
    <h2>Segmented view toggle</h2>
    <p>A two-or-more-way view switch (e.g. map/gallery) — square, umber-bordered, filled solid <code>--umber</code>
      when a segment is active. This is the same square/flat direction <code>.btn</code> already uses, applied to a
      button *group* instead of a single button — no rounded corners anywhere, matching the BIS direction.
      Closest existing precedent in this codebase is <code>CatalunyaProgramMap.astro</code>'s province filter chips
      (<code>.prov-chip</code>), which already do square + umber-on-active; this section documents that same
      treatment as a reusable, named pattern instead of a one-off. It's also the pattern
      <a href="https://github.com/refibcn/bioregioning-earth-ui" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">bioregioning-earth-ui</a>
      shipped first (its map/gallery toggle was terracotta + rounded; restyled to this square/umber
      treatment 2026-08-12) and is being carried back here, the same way <a href="/design-system/badges">Badge</a>'s
      pill/square split originated on that surface before landing in the lab.</p>
    <div class="lab-toggle" role="group" aria-label="Example view toggle">
      <button class="lab-toggle-btn active" type="button">🗺️ Map</button>
      <button class="lab-toggle-btn" type="button">🗂️ Gallery</button>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--gap">doesn't exist — sketch only</span>
    <h2>Progress bar</h2>
    <p>Determinate — a filled track in <code>--primary</code>, flat (no radius) to match the BIS direction.</p>
    <div style="max-width: 24rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-4);">
      <div>
        <div class="lab-progress-label">
          <span>Funding round</span><span>62%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lab-progress-track"><div class="lab-progress-fill" style="width: 62%;"></div></div>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="lab-progress-label">
          <span>Upload</span><span>100%</span>
        </div>
        <div class="lab-progress-track"><div class="lab-progress-fill lab-progress-fill--done" style="width: 100%;"></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-section">
    <span class="lab-status lab-status--gap">doesn't exist — sketch only</span>
    <h2>Spinner</h2>
    <p>Indeterminate loading — for button-loading states and async panels (e.g. the map components while
      tiles/geojson load).</p>
    <div class="lab-spinner" aria-label="Loading" role="status"></div>
  </div>

  <div class="lab-note">
    <strong>Also not present at all</strong> — worth knowing these gaps exist even before someone needs them:
    accordion/disclosure, tooltip, modal/dialog, pagination, toast/notification. Listed here so they don't get
    silently invented ad hoc the first time a page needs one.
  </div>
</LabShell>

<style>
  .lab-tabs {
    display: flex;
    gap: var(--space-5);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  }
  .lab-tab {
    background: none;
    border: 0;
    border-bottom: 2px solid transparent;
    padding: var(--space-2) 0 var(--space-3);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: color var(--t-fast), border-color var(--t-fast);
  }
  .lab-tab:hover:not(:disabled) { color: var(--text-primary); }
  .lab-tab.active { color: var(--text-primary); border-bottom-color: var(--primary); font-weight: 600; }
  .lab-tab:disabled { color: var(--border-default); cursor: not-allowed; }

  .lab-toggle {
    display: inline-flex;
    gap: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    box-shadow: 0 4px 16px rgba(42, 24, 16, 0.1);
  }
  .lab-toggle-btn {
    padding: var(--space-2) var(--space-4);
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.03em;
    background: var(--bg);
    color: var(--text-muted);
    border: 0;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .lab-toggle-btn.active { background: var(--umber); color: var(--paper); font-weight: 500; }

  .lab-progress-label {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }
  .lab-progress-track {
    height: 0.5rem;
    background: var(--surface-1);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  }
  .lab-progress-fill { height: 100%; background: var(--primary); }
  .lab-progress-fill--done { background: var(--success); }

  .lab-spinner {
    width: 2rem;
    height: 2rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 3px solid var(--border-subtle);
    border-top-color: var(--primary);
    animation: lab-spin 800ms linear infinite;
  }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .lab-spinner { animation-duration: 2400ms; }
  }
  @keyframes lab-spin {
    to { transform: rotate(360deg); }
  }
</style>
